### Nine billing: walk through the whole surface.
### In IntelliJ, click the green arrow next to each request. Run them top to bottom.

@host = http://localhost:18081
@tenant = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@apiKey = REMOVED-LEAKED-KEY

### 0. Mint the tenant's API key. Needs the bootstrap secret the service was started with:
###    NINE_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET=dev-bootstrap ./gradlew bootRun
###    Copy "apiKey" from the response into @apiKey above. It is shown once.
POST {{host}}/admin/keys
Content-Type: application/json
X-Bootstrap-Secret: dev-bootstrap

{
  "tenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "label": "local dev"
}

### 0b. Without a key, everything under /v1 is 401 problem+json.
GET {{host}}/v1/tenants/{{tenant}}/balance

### 1. Report usage: 120 agent-seconds. Expect 201, chargedMinor 240 (2.40 GBP).
POST {{host}}/v1/usage
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "evt-001",
  "tenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "metric": "agent_seconds",
  "quantity": 120
}

### 2. Same event again. Expect 200, replayed: true, SAME transactionId, no second charge.
POST {{host}}/v1/usage
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "evt-001",
  "tenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "metric": "agent_seconds",
  "quantity": 120
}

### 3. Another metric. 3 seats at 9.00 GBP. Expect 201, chargedMinor 2700.
POST {{host}}/v1/usage
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "evt-002",
  "tenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "metric": "seats",
  "quantity": 3
}

### 4. Balance. Expect owedMinor 2940, display "29.40 GBP".
GET {{host}}/v1/tenants/{{tenant}}/balance
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 5. Ledger lines, newest first. Two transactions, four postings.
GET {{host}}/v1/tenants/{{tenant}}/ledger?limit=20
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 6. Unknown metric. Expect 422 application/problem+json, balance unchanged.
POST {{host}}/v1/usage
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "evt-003",
  "tenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "metric": "moon_landings",
  "quantity": 1
}

### 7. Bad request: blank eventId, quantity 0. Expect 400 naming both fields.
POST {{host}}/v1/usage
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "",
  "tenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "metric": "seats",
  "quantity": 0
}

### 8. Reverse a transaction. Paste a transactionId from step 5 below. Expect 201.
### Then rerun step 4: balance drops by that amount. Rerun step 5: lines grew, nothing deleted.
POST {{host}}/v1/ledger/PASTE-TRANSACTION-ID-HERE/reverse
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "tenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "idempotencyKey": "rev-001",
  "reason": "goodwill credit"
}

### 9. Reverse the same transaction again. Expect 409: a transaction is reversed once.
POST {{host}}/v1/ledger/PASTE-TRANSACTION-ID-HERE/reverse
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "tenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "idempotencyKey": "rev-002",
  "reason": "again"
}

### 10. Health.
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### 11. Reconciliation: run it now. Expect clean: true, findings: [].
POST {{host}}/v1/reconciliation/run
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 12. Recent reconciliation runs. The scheduled job also writes here every 15 minutes.
GET {{host}}/v1/reconciliation/runs
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 13. Findings of a run (paste an id from step 12). Empty on a healthy ledger.
GET {{host}}/v1/reconciliation/runs/1/findings
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
